      "side": 1,
      "message": "`std::make_unique\u003cSkStrikeSpec\u003e(strike-\u003estrikeSpec())` introduces a heap allocation during drawing/flushing (e.g. in `initBackendData` / `submitDraws`).\n\nMore importantly, retaining `SkStrikeSpec` keeps strong references to `sk_sp\u003cSkTypeface\u003e`, `sk_sp\u003cSkPathEffect\u003e`, and `sk_sp\u003cSkMaskFilter\u003e` for the entire lifetime of `TextBlobRedrawCoordinator`, preventing them from being freed when `SkStrikeCache` is purged.\n\nAdditionally, when `SkStrikeCache::purgeAll()` evicts the strike while the Slug is alive, post-draw deserialization fails because `MakeFromBuffer` expects the strike to be resident via `findStrike` instead of recreating/pinning it.\n\nSee tests `TextBlob_draw_releases_typeface_and_effects` and `Slug_draw_purge_strike_cache_then_serialize` in https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1393296",
      "revId": "2a1bd6f84b5d81737efd2abccb6af4e3638f5490",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
