      "side": 1,
      "message": "Placing `uint16_t fGlyphID` immediately before `SkPath` (and `SkDrawable*` in `IDOrDrawable` below) introduces 6 bytes of alignment padding on 64-bit platforms, adding ~50%–100% memory overhead per glyph. We could reorder or pack the fields to eliminate this padding.\n\nAlso, the comment above still references `prepareForPathDrawing` (which was removed), and the `IDOr...` naming might be worth updating since these are structs now rather than unions.",
      "revId": "2a1bd6f84b5d81737efd2abccb6af4e3638f5490",
